  "hardware": {
    "family": "NVIDIA DGX Spark / GB10",
    "testedMachine": "One DGX Spark with 128 GB unified memory",
    "notes": [
      "This version pins the SparkLing 0.1.1 image ghcr.io/enntity/atlas-sparkling:753fe2b286a6 (also :0.1.1; install tree 753fe2b286a6, Atlas 965128de1), addressed by its digest. Its build ran 8,827 engine tests with 0 failures.",
      "SparkLing 0.1.1 on one GB10, 2026-11-25, Spark weights, default profile (262,144 tokens, eight requests) and default drafting, nothing else on the GPU (Enntity/SparkLing results/2026-11-25-0.1.1/README.md): single stream 54.8 tok/s (mean of eight greedy prompts, 256 tokens, thinking off), drafted text equal to plain decode on 8 of 8; aggregate 54.6 / 65.7 / 81.1 / 104.4 tok/s at 1 / 2 / 4 / 8 clients, median time to first token 1.04 s at 8; 30 of 30 arithmetic word problems with thinking on; 10 of 10 single-tool calls; a red-to-blue clip, a counting clip as GIF and MP4, a 90 s 720p clip, an invoice and a grid all read correctly.",
      "In SparkLing's 0.1.0 comparison runs on the same Spark, vLLM's MTP x3 serving the same NVFP4A16 checkpoint read 40.2 tok/s single-stream and 44.6 / 59.2 / 68.8 / 109.2 at 1 / 2 / 4 / 8 clients, at an 8,192-token window.",
      "Spark drafts one token per step with the checkpoint's own MTP predictor (SPARKLING_DRAFTER=mtp) for one active request and decodes plainly from two (ATLAS_MTP_MAX_SEQS=1); Atlas verifies each draft with serial decode's arithmetic, so greedy text matches drafting off.",
      "Every mode serves Ling's full 262,144-token window from one latent KV pool (1.15 KB per token per layer). The default pool holds 2,200,304 tokens, 8.4 full windows; eight simultaneous 262,132-token prompts each recalled their key. Decode after 2K / 32K / 128K / 262K prompts: 44.4 / 40.6 / 34.9 / 27.9 tok/s. SparkLing 0.1.0's 131,072-token default held only 56,352 KV tokens in total.",
      "Profiles (SparkLing install/profiles, all BF16 KV in a shared latent pool, prefix caching, 2,048-token prefill chunks or 8,192 with NVFP4 prefill, ffmpeg video decoding on): default 8 requests at 0.89 GPU memory utilization, saver 1 request at 0.70, max 16 requests at 0.95, each at the model's full window. Requests the KV pool cannot hold yet wait rather than fail. The engine borrows the GB10 display carveout for the KV cache when no other Spark* server holds the shared lock /run/lock/sparkglm (mounted here); the default pool's per-layer buffers are too large for it, smaller pools use it. SparkLing's disk prefix cache stays off here (LLooM sets no SPARKLING_PREFIX_CACHE_GB).",
      "Strict serves the original checkpoint for reference. It does not fit in memory, so Atlas pages experts from the checkpoint on disk and decodes at about 2 tok/s; its KV pool stops at eight full windows so the rest of memory can cache those experts.",
      "Peak host memory was not measured per mode. LLooM reserves an estimate: saver 92 GB, default 115 GB, max 120 GB (0.70 / 0.89 / 0.95 GPU memory utilization). The container is capped at 114 GiB because a GB10 that runs out of shared memory hangs instead of killing a process. In the default and max modes little else should use this Spark's GPU memory.",
      "The engine serves 127.0.0.1:8897 (fixed by the image) with host networking, so only one SparkLing model runs at a time; its memory reservation keeps LLooM from starting the other beside it. Text, image and video input: OpenAI image_url parts and video_url parts (animated GIF decoded in-process, MP4 and WebM through the image's ffmpeg).",
      "Licenses: the Atlas engine and SparkLing's install tools run from the image and are AGPL-3.0-only (not included in LLooM). inclusionAI/Ling-3.2-air and primitive-ai/Ling-3.2-air-NVFP4A16 are MIT."
    ]
  },
